# Fork-owned files — the popup rewrite lives here.
#
# `merge=forkours` makes an upstream merge keep the fork's version instead of
# producing conflict markers. The driver has to be enabled per clone:
#
#     git config merge.forkours.driver true
#
# (`true` exits 0 without writing %A, so git keeps the current branch's copy.)
#
# `merge=forktheirs` is the opposite: it hands upstream's side the result, which is
# what package.json wants because the fork keeps no local package.json changes.
# Enable it with:
#
#     git config merge.forktheirs.driver "cp %B %A"
#
# The scheduled "Upstream sync" workflow sets both up automatically, then verifies
# that these paths are byte-identical to master after the merge and reports every
# upstream commit that touched them, so nothing upstream is dropped silently.
#
# Keep this list in sync with scripts/fork-owned-paths.txt.
# package.json carries no fork-only content on purpose (see README): the fork keeps
# upstream's own name/version/repository, so upstream's version is always the right
# answer and release commits never conflict.
package.json merge=forktheirs
README.md merge=forkours
src/ui/health.ts merge=forkours
src/ui/help.ts merge=forkours
src/ui/profiles.ts merge=forkours
